-- S23 Maharashtra prose — lenyadri
-- Verdict matrix: 7 go / 3 skip / 2 wait
-- Anchors: Girijatmaj — 6th Ashtavinayak in yatra order, ONLY cave-temple Ashtavinayak (inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 Hinayana Manmodi/Junnar group 2nd c BCE), ONLY NORTH-facing Ashtavinayak, 307 steps up Manmodi hills, ASI-protected complex, Pune 95km via Chakan-Junnar, Junnar 12km (Shivneri Fort/Shivaji birthplace), Ozar 10km. Lenyadri override: May=1 not 2 (heat+climb); Jul/Aug=skip (slippery basalt steps)

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('lenyadri', 1, 'go', 4, 'January at Lenyadri runs at the year-best window for the only cave-temple Ashtavinayak. Girijatmaj (the son-of-Parvati form — atmaj means son, Girija is Parvati) sits inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 in the Hinayana Manmodi-Junnar cave group (2nd century BCE), making this the only Ashtavinayak inside a rock-cut cave and the only one north-facing among the eight temples. The cave complex sits 307 steps up the basalt face of Manmodi hill in Junnar district, 95km from Pune. Daytime 14-28C, nights 8-10C — the 307-step climb workable any time of day with the basalt holding dry and cool. The ASI-protected Hinayana cave-group context (29 surrounding caves, mostly chaitya halls and vihara monastic cells) sits at year-best photographic clarity. The Junnar valley below visible from the cave-mouth platform. Standard darshan 5am-9pm. Combine with Ozar (10km), Shivneri Fort 12km (Shivaji''s birthplace 1630), or both in a single day from Pune. Sankashti Chaturthi early-month standard Tuesday density.', 'January year-best — Girijatmaj inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30, only cave-temple + only north-facing Ashtavinayak. 14-28C, 307 steps workable any time of day. ASI Hinayana group 2nd c BCE. Combine with Ozar 10km + Shivneri Fort 12km.', NULL),
('lenyadri', 2, 'go', 5, 'February at Lenyadri makes Maghi Ganesh Jayanti a peak event at the only cave-temple Ashtavinayak. The festival — Magh Shukla Chaturthi — falls Wednesday 4 February 2026. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 (Hinayana Manmodi-Junnar group, 2nd century BCE) receives the pre-dawn maha-abhishek ritual at 4am — pilgrims start climbing the 307 steps from 3am to make the 4am slot. The only north-facing Ashtavinayak attracts dedicated yatra-pilgrims who specifically time their visit for this configuration. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 3 February 2026 compounding pilgrim density. Daytime 16-30C — the 307-step climb workable through the day; afternoon climbs slightly warmer. The ASI-protected cave-group landscape sits clean. Combine with Ozar 10km in the same morning. Lodgings at Junnar ₹800-2,200 festival rates; some pilgrims base at Pune (95km) and day-trip. Book 2 weeks ahead.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 + Angarki Feb 3 at only cave-temple Ashtavinayak. Girijatmaj inside Buddhist Cave 7. Pilgrims climb 307 steps from 3am for 4am maha-abhishek. North-facing configuration unique among 8 Ashtavinayak. Combine with Ozar 10km.', NULL),
('lenyadri', 3, 'go', 4, 'March at Lenyadri holds clean conditions through the first three weeks; the 307-step Manmodi climb starts to feel the heat-ramp by final week. Gudi Padwa Thursday 19 March 2026 brings extended morning ritual at Girijatmaj. Daytime 20-33C, nights 14-16C. The 307-step climb fully workable pre-9am; afternoon climbs (3-5pm) workable with care; mid-day climbs (11am-2pm) get hot on the exposed basalt staircase. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 sits in the cool stone interior holding 28-30C through the day. The Manmodi-Junnar Hinayana cave-group context (29 surrounding caves) at full visual clarity. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard density. Combine with Ozar 10km in the same morning. The 95km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar runs 2.5 hours. Lodgings at Junnar ₹500-1,400. Last clean-comfort window for the 307-step climb before April compresses it to dawn-only.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 extended ritual at Girijatmaj. 20-33C first 3 weeks. 307 steps fully workable pre-9am, mid-day exposed basalt gets hot. Combine with Ozar 10km. Junnar lodgings ₹500-1,400. Last clean window before April.', NULL),
('lenyadri', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April at Lenyadri compresses to pre-7am operations only. Daytime 25-38C in the Junnar valley — the 307-step Manmodi climb on exposed basalt holds direct sun 8am-5pm; the staircase surface reaches 45-50C noon. Even the pre-7am dawn climb opens at 24C and reaches 30C by 8am summit. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 sits in cool stone interior holding 32-34C through the day — the cave structure provides good insulation but the climb up is the limiting factor. Pilgrim arrivals thin sharply through month; lodging rates at Junnar drop to ₹400-1,000. The committed pilgrim flow shifts to dawn-only — climb starts 5am, summit by 6am, descend by 8am before the basalt heats. Combine with Ozar 10km only as a paired pre-9am morning. The Ashtavinayak yatra circuit packages drop Lenyadri from April-May itineraries. Push to October.', 'April compresses to pre-7am operations. 307 steps on exposed basalt 45-50C noon. Climb starts 5am, summit 6am, descend by 8am. Combine with Ozar 10km only as paired pre-9am morning. Ashtavinayak circuit drops Lenyadri Apr-May.', 'April runs at fragmented schedule. 307-step Manmodi climb on exposed basalt impossible past 7am. Most yatra packages drop Lenyadri from Apr-May itineraries. The full cave-temple experience compresses to a brief dawn fragment.'),
('lenyadri', 5, 'skip', 1, 'May is the worst Lenyadri month — score 1, lower than the other Ashtavinayak temples due to the 307-step climb compounding the heat. Daytime 29-41C in the Junnar valley; the basalt staircase surface hits 52-55C noon and holds direct sun 7am-6pm. Even the pre-6am dawn climb opens at 27C and reaches 33C by 7am summit. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 sits in cool stone interior holding 33-35C — the cave structure insulates well but reaching it from the basalt-step ascent is physically punishing. Heat-related incidents at Lenyadri spike in May — local pilgrim trust runs an emergency-water station mid-staircase from April onward. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 but most committed pilgrims skip Lenyadri specifically through May. The 95km Pune drive remains drivable; the climb itself is the failure point. ASI considers temporary climb restrictions during peak heat days. Lodgings drop to ₹400-1,000. Push to October.', NULL, 'May year-worst — 29-41C with 307 basalt steps reaching 52-55C surface noon. Even pre-6am climb opens at 27C. Heat incidents spike. ASI considers temporary climb restrictions. Most yatra packages skip Lenyadri through May. Score 1, lowest of any month.'),
('lenyadri', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks southwest monsoon arrival in Lenyadri. First-week rains break the heat — daytime 21-31C, nights 18-20C. The 307-step Manmodi climb becomes weather-dependent. Wet basalt steps hold zero grip — the climb workable on dry mornings only, treacherous within 30 minutes of any rainfall. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 sits in fresh post-rain visual context — the Manmodi cave-group landscape with green-cover return after the long dry stretch is photographically striking. ASI staff post wet-step warnings from mid-June onward. The 95km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar takes 2.5-3 hours through monsoon delays. Sankashti Chaturthi late month — dedicated pilgrims attempt the climb on confirmed-dry-day weather windows. Pilgrim lodging at Junnar ₹500-1,300 with monsoon discount. Combine with Ozar 10km only on confirmed weather-dry mornings; the joint operating window is narrow.', 'June monsoon arrival — 21-31C, fresh post-rain visual context at Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 Manmodi group. 307 steps workable on dry mornings only — wet basalt zero grip. Confirmed-dry weather windows essential. Combine with Ozar 10km.', 'June transition month — 307 wet basalt steps treacherous within 30 min of rain. ASI staff post wet-step warnings mid-month. Operating window narrow — must confirm dry-morning weather before climb attempt.'),
('lenyadri', 7, 'skip', 2, 'July is unsafe Lenyadri. Monsoon-peak rainfall in the Junnar valley — 400-550mm through the month; the basalt 307-step Manmodi climb holds rainwater on the exposed staircase and the lower 100 steps overflow as a brief waterfall on heavy-rain days. Wet basalt holds zero grip — slip-and-fall incidents spike in July. ASI typically posts advisory closure of the cave-climb on heavy-rain days. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 sits inaccessible to most pilgrims through July; only emergency-dry-window climbs succeed. The Ozar 10km combination collapses operationally — pilgrims focus on Ozar alone and skip Lenyadri. The Ashtavinayak yatra package operators (MTDC, MSRTC, private) drop Lenyadri from July itineraries explicitly. The 95km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar takes 2.5-3 hours through caution sections. Sankashti Chaturthi pilgrim flow modest. Push to September festival window or October post-monsoon.', NULL, 'July monsoon peak — 307 basalt steps overflow as brief waterfall on heavy rain days, zero grip. ASI advisory closure typical. Yatra package operators drop Lenyadri from July itineraries explicitly. Slip-fall incidents spike. Cave-7 Girijatmaj inaccessible. Push to September or October.'),
('lenyadri', 8, 'skip', 2, 'August holds monsoon-peak conditions at Lenyadri — the 307-step Manmodi climb remains physically dangerous. Wet basalt continues at zero grip. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 4 August 2026 — committed yatra-pilgrims accept the risk; the ASI cave-trust runs additional emergency staff on Aug 4 to support the Angarki pilgrim flow, but standard climb advisory remains in effect on heavy-rain days. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 visited by far fewer pilgrims than the surrounding Ashtavinayak temples through August. Most yatra packages continue to drop Lenyadri from August itineraries. The Ozar 10km combination collapses operationally. Daytime 21-30C, humid; rainfall sustained at 300-450mm. The 95km Pune drive takes 2.5-3 hours. Lodgings at Junnar ₹500-1,400. Pre-Ganesh-Chaturthi build through final week brings dedicated pilgrim flow regardless of conditions. Push to September festival window.', NULL, 'August continues monsoon peak — 307 wet basalt steps remain at zero grip and slip-fall risk. Angarki Aug 4 pilgrims accept risk but ASI advisory closure typical on heavy rain. Yatra packages drop Lenyadri from itineraries. Push to September festival window.'),
('lenyadri', 9, 'go', 5, 'September makes Lenyadri a Ganesh Chaturthi anchor — and the post-monsoon reopening of the 307-step Manmodi climb. The festival (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 — the only cave-temple Ashtavinayak — receives continuous palki processions through the festival; the dindi pilgrim groups carry the procession down and back up the 307 steps in scheduled relay teams. The cave-mouth platform handles the festival density. The 307 basalt steps reopen as weather clears mid-month; ASI staff resume normal operations by Anant Chaturdashi. Daytime 22-30C with monsoon tail rains tapering through first week. The 95km Pune drive takes 3-3.5 hours through festival traffic. Lodgings at Junnar book 90 days ahead at ₹1,500-3,500 festival rates. Combine with Ozar 10km Day 2.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 — Girijatmaj in Buddhist Cave 7 at festival saturation. Dindi processions on 307-step relay. Monsoon tapers, climb reopens by Anant Chaturdashi. Junnar lodgings ₹1,500-3,500. Combine with Ozar 10km Day 2.', NULL),
('lenyadri', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is post-monsoon ideal Lenyadri. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed; the 307-step Manmodi climb at year-best traction — freshly washed basalt grips cleanly underfoot. Daytime 18-31C, nights 15-17C. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 (the ASI Hinayana Manmodi-Junnar group, 2nd century BCE) sits in cleanest visual presentation — the post-monsoon green cover on the Manmodi hillside contrasts with the bare basalt cave-mouth. The wider Hinayana cave-group context (29 surrounding caves, chaitya halls and vihara cells) at peak photographic clarity. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 bringing dedicated pilgrim density without the September overload. Combine with Ozar 10km in the same morning at year-best traction. The 95km Pune drive returns to 2.5-hour standard time. Lodgings at Junnar ₹700-1,800. Combine with Shivneri Fort 12km for Shivaji-birthplace extension.', 'Post-monsoon ideal — 18-31C, 307 steps at year-best traction with freshly washed basalt. Buddhist Cave 7 Girijatmaj + ASI Hinayana group at peak visual. Angarki Tue Oct 6. Combine with Ozar 10km + Shivneri Fort 12km (Shivaji birthplace).', NULL),
('lenyadri', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Lenyadri stretch. The post-monsoon Junnar-valley green holds through first two weeks; daytime 15-29C, nights 11-13C — the sharpest cool weather of the year. The 307-step Manmodi climb workable any time of day at year-best basalt traction. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 sits in cleanest visual presentation; the ASI Hinayana Manmodi-Junnar cave-group context (29 surrounding caves from the 2nd century BCE) at peak clarity. The only north-facing Ashtavinayak configuration receives the cool dry winter light against the cave structure distinctively. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard Tuesday density. The 95km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar runs cleanest of the year — 2.5 hours on weekday mornings. Pilgrim lodgings at Junnar ₹700-1,800. Combine with Ozar 10km + Shivneri Fort 12km (Shivaji-birthplace) for a comprehensive Junnar heritage day.', 'November year-best — 15-29C, sharpest cool. 307 steps at peak traction. Buddhist Cave 7 Girijatmaj + ASI Hinayana group at cleanest visual. Only north-facing Ashtavinayak. Combine with Ozar 10km + Shivneri Fort 12km. 95km Pune drive 2.5 hours.', NULL),
('lenyadri', 12, 'go', 4, 'December at Lenyadri opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 1 December 2026, the auspicious month-opener pulling dedicated pilgrim flow. The 307-step Manmodi climb at strong winter traction; pilgrims start 4-5am for the dawn slot. The Girijatmaj murti inside Buddhist Cave 7 of 30 runs full ritual schedule. Daytime 13-28C, nights 7-9C — year-coolest stretch; light woolens essential for the pre-dawn climb. The ASI Hinayana Manmodi-Junnar cave-group context at clean visual presentation. The 95km Pune drive via Chakan-Junnar runs heavy weekend traffic through Pune-tourist-escape season — 15 percent longer through December weekends. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard flow. Combine with Ozar 10km in the same morning + Shivneri Fort 12km. Pilgrim lodgings at Junnar rise to ₹800-2,000 at year-end peak. Book mid-month weekdays for cleanest experience.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi opens strong. 13-28C year-coolest. 307 steps at strong winter traction. Buddhist Cave 7 Girijatmaj at clean visual. Combine with Ozar 10km + Shivneri Fort 12km. Lodgings ₹800-2,000.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
  why_go = EXCLUDED.why_go,
  why_not = EXCLUDED.why_not;
